8. Dominance conditions

8.1 Setup

Assumption 1 (CIA). $P_t = M_t / Y_t$.
Assumption 2 (Log-differences). $\pi_t = \Delta \log P_t$, $\Delta m_t = \Delta \log M_t$, $\Delta y_t = \Delta \log Y_t$.

8.2 Decomposition

Theorem 5. With $\mu_m = \mathbb{E}[\Delta m]$, $\mu_y = \mathbb{E}[\Delta y]$:
\mathbb{E}[(\pi_t - \pi^*)^2] = \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m) + \operatorname{Var}(\Delta y) - 2 \operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m, \Delta y) + (\mu_m - \mu_y - \pi^*)^2

Proof. $\pi_t = \Delta m_t - \Delta y_t$. Then $\operatorname{Var}(\pi_t) = \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m) + \operatorname{Var}(\Delta y) - 2\operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m, \Delta y)$, and $\mathbb{E}[\pi_t] - \pi^* = \mu_m - \mu_y - \pi^*$. Combine. $\square$

8.3 Dominance condition

Corollary 1. $L_P^{(C2)} < L_F^{(C2)}$ iff:
\left[\operatorname{Var}(\Delta m^C) - \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m^F)\right] - 2\left[\operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m^C, \Delta y) - \operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m^F, \Delta y)\right] + \left[(\mu_m^C - \mu_y - \pi^*)^2 - (\mu_m^F - \mu_y - \pi^*)^2\right] < 0

[v3.1] Remark 8. $\operatorname{Var}(\Delta y)$ is not cancelled. $\Delta y$ is endogenous to the monetary regime through the chain of §5. The dominance condition as stated contains all relevant terms.

[v3.1] Remark 9 (Where compute and capital enter). Through $P_t^{\text{phys}}$ (Theorem 2), through $K_{t+1}, C_{t+1}$ dynamics (§5.2–5.3), and through $\mu_m^C$ in the drift bracket. If compute grows exponentially, $\mu_m^C$ drifts up, and the drift bracket penalizes the capacity rule.

