9. Loss function

Definition 4.
L = w_\pi \mathbb{E}[(\pi_t - \pi^*)^2] + w_y \mathbb{E}[\tilde{Y}_t^2] + w_i \operatorname{Var}(i_t) + w_c \Pr(\text{crisis})

Crisis: $|\pi - \pi^*| > 5$ pp or $\tilde{Y} < -5\%$. Thresholds pre-registered.

$u_t$ dropped: no labor block in v0.1.

Weight grid (pre-registered).
w_\pi = 1, \quad w_y \in \{0.25, 0.5, 1\}, \quad w_i \in \{0, 0.1\}, \quad w_c \in \{0, 1\}


12 combinations, applied uniformly.

Pareto vector.
\mathbf{L} = (\mathbb{E}[(\pi - \pi^*)^2], \mathbb{E}[\tilde{Y}^2], \operatorname{Var}(i), \Pr(\text{crisis})) \in \mathbb{R}^4_+

