11. Falsifiable hypotheses

H1. $q_{P,C1} \geq 0.75$ with bootstrap 95% CI excluding 0.5.

H2. $\tau^*$ stable under $\pm 20\%$ perturbation; train/test gap on $L_P$ statistically insignificant.

H3. $q_{P,c} > 0.5$ for each $c \in \{C1, C2, C3\}$.

[v3.1] H4. Let $\rho_{C,Y}(\theta)$ be the correlation between filter-implied compute growth and the output gap under calibration $\theta$. Then:
\boxed{ \frac{\partial q_P}{\partial |\rho_{C,Y}|} < 0 }


The win-share decreases as compute becomes more cycle-correlated. Estimated by regressing $q_P$ on $|\rho_{C,Y}|$ across draws, with a bootstrap CI.

H5. The anchor's advantage is not sensitive to $\kappa_\varepsilon$ on $[0.8, 1.2]$, but is destroyed if $\omega$ pushes composition strongly toward services.

