Appendix H — Proof of Theorem 5 (Variance-and-drift decomposition)

Theorem H.1 (restatement of Theorem 5). Under Assumptions 1–2 (CIA, log-differences), with $\mu_m = \mathbb{E}[\Delta m]$, $\mu_y = \mathbb{E}[\Delta y]$, and $\pi^* \in \mathbb{R}$:
\mathbb{E}[(\pi_t - \pi^*)^2] = \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m) + \operatorname{Var}(\Delta y) - 2\operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m, \Delta y) + (\mu_m - \mu_y - \pi^*)^2.

Proof.

From $P_t Y_t = M_t$, taking logs: $p_t + y_t = m_t$. Differencing: $\pi_t + \Delta y_t = \Delta m_t$, so
\pi_t = \Delta m_t - \Delta y_t.

Variance. $\operatorname{Var}(\pi_t) = \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m_t - \Delta y_t) = \operatorname{Var}(\Delta m) + \operatorname{Var}(\Delta y) - 2\operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m, \Delta y)$.

Mean. $\mathbb{E}[\pi_t] = \mu_m - \mu_y$. Therefore $\mathbb{E}[\pi_t] - \pi^* = \mu_m - \mu_y - \pi^*$.

Combination. By the identity $\mathbb{E}[(X - c)^2] = \operatorname{Var}(X) + (\mathbb{E}[X] - c)^2$ with $X = \pi_t$, $c = \pi^*$:
\mathbb{E}[(\pi_t - \pi^*)^2] = \operatorname{Var}(\pi_t) + (\mathbb{E}[\pi_t] - \pi^*)^2.


Substituting:
= [\operatorname{Var}(\Delta m) + \operatorname{Var}(\Delta y) - 2\operatorname{Cov}(\Delta m, \Delta y)] + (\mu_m - \mu_y - \pi^*)^2. \quad \square

Remark H.1. $\operatorname{Var}(\Delta y)$ is retained in the decomposition. It is not cancelled in the difference $L_P - L_F$ of Appendix I because $\Delta y$ is regime-endogenous (§5 dynamics of $K, C$ feed back to $Y$).

